<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Vorexa</title>
<meta name="description" content="Vorexa — replace this with a one-line description of what you do.">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>

<header class="masthead">
  <div class="shell masthead__inner">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/">
      <span class="wordmark__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      Vorexa
    </a>
    <nav class="masthead__nav" aria-label="Main">
      <a href="/" aria-current="page">Home</a>
      <a href="/contact.html">Contact</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<main>

  <section class="shell lede">
    <h1>Your site is live.</h1>
    <p>
      If you can read this, the deployment is working and the 404 is gone.
      Replace this page with your real content — the file layout underneath is
      already the one Vercel expects.
    </p>
    <p class="meta-line">
      <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      Served from the repository root
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact.html">Go to the contact page</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#layout">See the file layout</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell ruled" id="layout">
    <div>
      <h2>index.html</h2>
      <p>
        This file. It has to sit at the top level of the repository, not inside
        a folder. Vercel serves it as the homepage with no configuration at all.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>contact.html</h2>
      <p>
        Reachable at <code>/contact.html</code>. Any extra pages work the same
        way — add the file, and the path follows the filename.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>styles.css</h2>
      <p>
        Linked from both pages with a leading slash, so the path resolves from
        the site root rather than the current page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell lede lede--tight">
    <h1>Keep the settings empty.</h1>
    <p>
      With Framework Preset set to Other and no build command, Vercel serves
      these files directly. Leave Root Directory and Output Directory blank.
      There is nothing to build, so there is nothing to misconfigure.
    </p>
  </section>

</main>

<footer class="foot">
  <div class="shell foot__inner">
    <span>Vorexa</span>
    <nav aria-label="Footer">
      <a href="/contact.html">Contact</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
